      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shawville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "It sits on the West Branch Susquehanna River where Pennsylvania Routes 879 and 970 cross, just 5.1 miles northeast of Clearfield.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shawville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Shawville Generating Station, once a 626‑MW coal plant operated by GenOn Energy, switched to 590‑MW natural gas in December 2016.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shawville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 2011 environmental investigation ranked Shawville third in the United States for toxic emissions per power station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shawville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Clearfield County, where Shawville is located, was established on March 26, 1804, and was named for the clear fields seen by early travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitclearfieldcounty.org/historical_sites"
    },
    {
